sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User
    participant B as Browser / Client App
    participant S as Authorization Server

    Note over B,S: ⚠ Deviation from RFC 6749: no GET /authorize redirect -<br/>credentials are submitted directly by the browser in the same POST request.

    rect rgb(220, 240, 255)
    Note over B,S: Registration (custom pre-step - one-time)
    B->>S: POST /oauth/pkce/register { client_id, password }
    S-->>B: 201 { status: registered }
    end

    rect rgb(220, 255, 220)
    Note over U,S: Authorization Code Grant + PKCE S256  (RFC 6749 + RFC 7636)
    U->>B: Click login
    Note over B: Generate code_verifier (random urlsafe)<br/>code_challenge = BASE64URL(SHA-256(code_verifier))
    B-->>U: Show login form
    U->>B: Enter { username, password }
    B->>S: POST /oauth/pkce/authorize<br/>{ response_type: code, client_id,<br/>  redirect_uri, username, password,<br/>  code_challenge, code_challenge_method: S256,<br/>  scope, state }
    S-->>B: 200 { code, state, redirect_uri, expires_in, scope }
    end

    rect rgb(244, 242, 245)
    Note over B,S: Token Exchange  (RFC 6749 §4.1.3 + RFC 7636 §4.5)
    B->>S: POST /oauth/pkce/token<br/>{ grant_type: authorization_code,<br/>  code, client_id, redirect_uri,<br/>  code_verifier }
    Note over S: Verify PKCE: BASE64URL(SHA-256(code_verifier)) == stored code_challenge
    S-->>B: 200 { access_token (JWT Bearer),<br/>  token_type: Bearer, expires_in: 3600,<br/>  refresh_token, scope }
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 220)
    Note over B,S: Token Refresh  (RFC 6749 §6)
    B->>S: POST /oauth/pkce/token<br/>{ grant_type: refresh_token,<br/>  refresh_token, client_id }
    S-->>B: 200 { access_token (JWT Bearer),<br/>  token_type: Bearer, expires_in: 3600,<br/>  refresh_token, scope }
    end
